body:
Execute Ticket 4 (t-run2-w4-doctor-install-sidecar) for Release Audit Run 2.

IMPORTANT HEADLESS WORKER RULES:
- Use ONLY view_file, replace_file_content, and write_to_file.
- Do NOT call run_command (the scheduler automatically runs the test suite in the gating phase immediately after you finish editing).
- Only edit files in your declared scope.

1. In lib/doctor.mjs (SHOULD-FIX #8 & BACKLOG #5):
   - Note: isTestExecution(env = process.env) is ALREADY defined at line 792 of lib/doctor.mjs. Do NOT import it.
   - In checkKernelContainment(platform = process.platform, options = {}) (lines 1062-1067), gate AGB_MOCK_CONTAINMENT_UNAVAILABLE and AGB_MOCK_CONTAINMENT_MECHANISM behind if (isTestExecution(env)), preserving the exact return objects:
     if (isTestExecution(env)) {
       if (env.AGB_MOCK_CONTAINMENT_UNAVAILABLE === '1') {
         return { supported: false, mechanism: null, kind: 'mock_unavailable', detail: 'Kernel containment floor unavailable (mocked)' };
       }
       if (env.AGB_MOCK_CONTAINMENT_MECHANISM) {
         return { supported: true, mechanism: env.AGB_MOCK_CONTAINMENT_MECHANISM };
       }
     }
   - In checkAgyAuth (lines 63-66), single-quote cmd before interpolating into script -c on Linux:
     if (process.platform === 'linux') {
       const quotedCmd = `'${String(cmd).replace(/'/g, "'\\''")}'`;
       args = ['-q', '-e', '-c', `${quotedCmd} models`, '/dev/null'];
       cmd = 'script';
     }

2. In sidecars/jetski-launcher.mjs, sidecars/app.js, and sidecars/style.css (SHOULD-FIX #7 & BACKLOG #12):
   - In sidecars/jetski-launcher.mjs (lines 60-95), align /events with sidecars/server.mjs:
     * Track let isReset = false; if (offset > stats.size) { offset = 0; isReset = true; }
     * Ensure result includes newOffset: offset and ...(isReset ? { reset: true } : {}) even when stats.size === 0.
     * Read in a while (totalRead < buffer.length) loop up to MAX_CHUNK = 1024 * 1024.
     * If lastNewline === -1 and offset + toRead < stats.size, set result = { lines: [buffer.toString('utf8', 0, toRead)], newOffset: offset + toRead, runId, repo: repoPath, reset: isReset, warning: 'Dropped oversized line' }.
     * If lastNewline !== -1, track droppedCorrupt on invalid JSON lines and set result = { lines, newOffset: offset + lastNewline + 1, runId, repo: repoPath, reset: isReset, ...(droppedCorrupt ? { warning: 'Dropped unparseable JSON line' } : {}) }.
   - In sidecars/app.js:
     * Preserve 'run-status' base class whenever setting runStatus.className (lines 42, 69, 72, 77, 80): e.g. 'run-status status-badge status-running' and 'run-status status-badge status-failed'.
     * Replace var(--color-status-failed) with var(--danger) on lines 68, 76, 79.
     * In processEvent(evt), when an active event (evt.type === 'pool' || evt.type === 'phase' || evt.type === 'strike') is processed and !state.done and runStatus.innerHTML.includes('Waiting for activity...'), set runStatus.innerHTML = '<span class="pulse"></span>Running...';
   - In sidecars/style.css:
     * Add --color-status-failed: var(--danger); in :root.

3. In lib/migrate.mjs and lib/bootstrap.mjs (BACKLOG #6 & #7):
   - In lib/migrate.mjs:428 (handOverUninstall), include ...(isWin ? { USERPROFILE: home } : {}) in childEnv:
     const childEnv = { ...process.env, HOME: home, ...(isWin ? { USERPROFILE: home } : {}), ...(ctx.uninstallerEnv ?? {}) };
   - In lib/bootstrap.mjs:191 (installReason), keep "function installReason(r, forceReinstall)" (do NOT add export!) and replace r.dir.split('/').pop() with basename(r.dir) (adding basename to the import from 'node:path' on line 2).

4. Add a unit test at the end of test/doctor.test.mjs (using NODE_ENV: 'production' in env to test checkKernelContainment ignoring mocks outside test mode).
